
  <sn><md>#### Carbohydrates

Introduction &amp; Definition

* **Chemical Composition:** Carbohydrates are organic compounds composed of `CHO` **Carbon (C)**, **Hydrogen (H)**, and **Oxygen (O)**. Because of this composition, they are often referred to as `hydrates of carbon`.
* **Exact Definition:** Carbohydrates are defined as `polyhydroxy aldehydes` or `polyhydroxy ketones`, or substances that yield these compounds upon hydrolysis (breakdown with water).
[view](https://i.ytimg.com/vi/hWmnXbfBnhc/maxresdefault.jpg)
* **Empirical Formula:** Many carbohydrates follow the general formula $\text{C}_n(\text{H}_2\text{O})_n$, though some may also contain `Nitrogen, Phosphorus, or Sulfur`.
* **Nomenclature:** Carbohydrates are also called `saccharides`, derived from the Greek word *sakkcharon*, meaning sugar or sweet.
</md></sn>
