<sn><md>### Structural Features

Functional Groups
Carbohydrates `contain specific functional groups` attached to a long carbon chain:

:::.row
:::.col-12 .col-lg-6
* **Polyhydroxy Aldehyde:** A long carbon chain attached to an `aldehyde group` -$\text{CHO}$. 
  * *Example:* **Glucose** $\text{C}_6\text{H}_{12}\text{O}_6$ — an *Aldohexose*.

* **Polyhydroxy Ketone:** A long carbon chain attached to a `ketone group` &gt;$\text{C}=\text{O}$. 
  * *Example:* **Fructose** $\text{C}_6\text{H}_{12}\text{O}_6$ — a *Ketohexose*.

* **Identification:** To qualify as a carbohydrate, a chemical structure must contain both a carbonyl group (aldehyde or ketone) and hydroxyl $-\text{OH}$ groups.
[view](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Soil%20Biochemistry/Carbohydrate/assets/carbohydrate_identifications.png)
