</md></sn><sn><md>### Monosaccharides 

Simple Sugars

* **Definition:** The simplest group of carbohydrates consisting of a `single` polyhydroxy aldehyde or ketone unit. They **cannot be further hydrolyzed** into smaller carbohydrates.

  +++ ...
  ![img](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Soil%20Biochemistry/Carbohydrate/assets/family_of_monosacarrides.yt.png)
  +++

* **Classification by Functional Group**:
  * `Aldoses`: Contain an `aldehyde` functional group (e.g., *Glyceraldehyde, Erythrose, Ribose, Glucose, Galactose*).
  * `Ketoses`: Contain a `ketone` functional group (e.g., *Dihydroxyacetone, Erythrulose, Ribulose, Fructose, Sedoheptulose*).

* **Classification by Carbon Count**:
  +++view
  | Carbon Count | Aldoses (Aldehyde Group) | Ketoses (Ketone Group) |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | **Trioses (3C)** | Glyceraldehyde | Dihydroxyacetone |
  | **Tetroses (4C)** | Erythrose | Erythrulose |
  | **Pentoses (5C)** | Ribose | Ribulose |
  | **Hexoses (6C)** | Glucose, Galactose | Fructose |
  | **Heptoses (7C)** | - | Sedoheptulose |
  +++

* **Key Monosaccharides Compared**:
  +++ view
  ![diagram](https://bio.libretexts.org/@api/deki/files/925/Figure_03_02_02.jpg?revision=1)
  ![diff.diagram](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Nh-emon/QDoc/main/SES3/Soil%20Biochemistry/Carbohydrate/assets/sucrose_galactose_fructose_diff_diagram.jpeg)
  +++
  * **Glucose:** The `primary energy source` for the body $1\text{ molecule} \rightarrow 36\text{–}38\text{ ATP }$; present in `blood` and tested in blood sugar panels.
  * **Galactose:** Derived from `lactose breakdown`; found predominantly in `dairy products`.
  * **Fructose:** The `sweetest natural sugar`; found in `fruits` and present in the `sperm head` as an *energy fuel* for motility. 

