</md></sn><sn><md>### Oligosaccharides

* **Definition:** Carbohydrates consisting of `3 to 10` monosaccharide units joined by *glycosidic bonds*.

* **Key Examples**:
  | Oligosaccharide | Category | Unit Count | Monosaccharide Composition |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | **Raffinose** `gGf` | Trisaccharide | 3 | Galactose + Glucose + Fructose |
  | **Stachyose** `2gGF` | Tetrasaccharide | 4 | 2 Galactose + Glucose + Fructose |
  | **Verbascose** `3gGf` | Pentasaccharide | 5 | 3 Galactose + Glucose + Fructose |* 
  [Raffinose](https://www.nutrientsreview.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/08/Oligosaccharides.jpg)
  
**Biological Significance:** Found in plant foods like `legumes, vegetables, and whole grains`. 
  They resist upper GI digestion and pass into the colon, where gut bacteria (`Bifidobacterium`, `Lactobacillus`) ferment them into **Short-Chain Fatty Acids (SCFAs)** and gases. They act as `prebiotics`.
</md></sn><sn><md>### Polysaccharides 

Complex Carbohydrates

* **Definition:** High molecular weight carbohydrates made of `more than 10 monosaccharide units` linked by glycosidic bonds.

* **1. Homopolysaccharides** 
  Composed of identical monosaccharide units:
  | Polysaccharide | Constituent Units | Primary Biological Role | Key Location / Occurrence |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | **Starch** | Glucose units | Energy storage | Plants |
  | **Glycogen** | Glucose units | Energy storage | Animals |
  | **Cellulose** | Glucose units | Structural support | Plant cell walls |
  | **Chitin** | *N-acetylglucosamine* units | Structural support &amp; protection | Insect exoskeletons and fungal cell walls |

* **2. Heteropolysaccharides** 
  Composed of two or more different types of monosaccharides:
  * **Hyaluronic Acid:** Made of alternating `Glucuronic acid` and `N-acetylglucosamine`; abundant in **connective tissue**.
  * **Heparin:** An `anticoagulant` agent.
  * **Agar:** Composed of galactose units and other sugar derivatives; derived from `seaweed` and used as a solidifying agent in microbiology culture media.

</md></sn><sn><md>### Summary Table

| Category | Sugar Units | Key Examples | Biological Role / Source |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Monosaccharides** | 1 | Glucose, Fructose, Galactose | Primary cellular fuel (36–38 ATP), semen fuel, milk derivative |
| **Disaccharides** | 2 | Sucrose, Lactose, Maltose | Table sugar, milk sugar, malt sugar |
| **Oligosaccharides** | 3–10 | Raffinose, Stachyose, Verbascose | Prebiotics, fermented by gut microbiota |
| **Polysaccharides** | &gt;10 | Starch, Glycogen, Cellulose, Chitin, Hyaluronic Acid, Agar | Energy storage, structural support, connective tissue, culture media |
</md></sn>